#---
# purpose: repeating a 10-byte string 2,000,001 times writes the 20 MB result into one shared buffer of exactly its size
# kind: run
#---
#
# The program prints the size of the result, then the shared buffers
# `String.duplicate` allocated and their total bytes.
a = Process.heap_alloc_stats()
big = String.duplicate("abcdefghij", 2_000_001)
z = Process.heap_alloc_stats()
dbg(byte_size(big))
dbg({z[:shared_bin_allocs] - a[:shared_bin_allocs], z[:shared_bin_bytes] - a[:shared_bin_bytes]})
